From 57dd5c907fd4c4adc60351fe24eea543eed0195a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 19:16:11 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] video: drm: Enable A733 HDMI scanout and simplefb Linux
 handoff

- Power on PCK600 R_PPU power domains 1 (DE_SYS), 9 (VO/TCON3), and 10 (VO1/HDMI).
- Add AXP8191 PMIC regulator mappings for DCDC2 (0.8V) and CLDO1-5 / DLDO1-2,
  wiring DCDC2 and CLDO2 (1.8V) to HDMI and PHY supplies.
- Un-gate and deassert VO1, DPSS_TOP1, TCON_TV0, and DW-HDMI clocks and resets.
- Wire DM_VIDEO pre-allocated framebuffer plat->base directly to
  drm_framebuffer_alloc() rather than allocating dynamically from the low heap.
- Truncate DRAM Bank 0 at plat->base via fdt_fixup_memory_banks() and increase
  FDT blob buffer size so simplefb handoff to Linux simpledrm succeeds without
  ioremap RAM conflict or FDT_ERR_NOSPACE errors.
- Add mode selection fallback to first probed mode or 1080p60 default when no
  probed mode has the PREFERRED flag set.
- Fix black/invisible screen issue by defaulting overlay blend mode to
  DRM_MODE_BLEND_PIXEL_NONE so DE3.5 ignores zero pixel-alpha and renders text/pixels
  at full opacity, and hand off x8r8g8b8 to Linux simplefb/simpledrm.
- Expand CCU gates/resets count to u16.

Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
